"concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": null}, {"id": "claude_conventional_commits", "label": "Conventional Commits 1.0.0 convention", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "'perf' is reserved for changes whose point is an SLO/latency/throughput improvement, with before/after numbers in the body, so `git log --grep '^perf'` becomes the history of what actually moved the needle \u2014 distinguishing it from 'feat' for new capability."}, {"id": "claude_graphify_terraform_extra", "label": "graphify[terraform] extra", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Marked mandatory because without it 30 .tf, 2 .hcl and 1 .tfvars file (33 of 81 code files, in a repo about Terraform) index as nothing, and graphify only warns rather than failing \u2014 so an incomplete map looks exactly like a complete one."}, {"id": "claude_graphify_semantic_cache", "label": "graphify-out/cache/semantic", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Committed (unlike the rest of graphify-out/) so the paid LLM extraction work is shared rather than repeated per clone: a warm cache rebuilt the full graph in 0.95s versus 10m43s cold, with zero LLM calls; CI regenerates it on master so git pull is usually enough."}, {"id": "claude_piib_flow", "label": "PIIB (present it in browser)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A decision answered from a terminal prompt is answered from memor